<title>USA: Thornburg Mortgage sees assets rising.</title>
<headline>Thornburg Mortgage sees assets rising.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA FE, N.M. 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thornburg Mortgage Asset Corp said on Wednesday that it expected total assets to top $3.5 billion by June 30, up from $3.27 billion in assets reported on March 31.</p>
<p>Thornburg president Larry Goldstone said the increase was anticipated in light of continued strong asset growth. For the year-end figure reported on December 31, the company posted assets of $2.75 billion, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>Thornburg is a special purpose mortgage company.</p>
</text>
